{
	"addonId": "selectionInfo",
	"displayName": "Selection Info – Detailed analysis of selected text",
	"URL": "https://github.com/kasturibhosale2207-svg/selectionAnnouncer/releases/download/v1.0/selectionInfo-1.0.nvda-addon",
	"description": "Provides comprehensive information about selected text with multiple shortcut keys, each supporting multiple presses to cycle through features.\n\nShortcuts:\n• Ctrl+Shift+A – Character count (1st press), word count (2nd), line count (3rd)\n• Ctrl+Shift+Q – Sentence count (1st), longest and shortest words (2nd), number/digit count (3rd)\n• Ctrl+Shift+E – Copy to clipboard (1st), selected emails count (2nd), selection info (3rd), save to file (4th)\n• Ctrl+Shift+R – Copy only digits from selection\n• Ctrl+Shift+Y – Maths calculations: addition (1st), subtraction (2nd), multiplication (3rd), division (4th)\n• Ctrl+Shift+F – Announce and copy the last maths result\n• Ctrl+Shift+O – Extract URLs (1st), open extracted URLs in browser (2nd)\n• Ctrl+Shift+V – Play/stop voice guide (audio file must be present)\n\nAll features can be enabled/disabled in NVDA Settings → Selection Info.\nDouble‑press timeout and auto‑save location are also configurable.\nAuthor: Kasturi Bhosale\nMinimum NVDA version: 2023, last tested: 2026.1",
	"sha256": "f9ba50d8d3c4e49bcbb8a057e44ff740e0adb11ea061b0b303d8fdc65c843800",
